# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env — it holds live credentials.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every tool here reads credentials from the environment first and this file
# second, so `export GHL_PIT=...` also works and takes precedence.

# ── Public API (services.leadconnectorhq.com, incl. the MCP server) ──────────
# Private Integration Token. Create it in the SUB-ACCOUNT:
#   Settings -> Private Integrations -> Create new integration
# Scope it to only what you need. It is a live credential.
# Used by: ghl_mcp.py, create_custom_values.py, create_form.py (--list)
GHL_PIT=pit-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# The sub-account (location) id. It is the 20-character id in your GHL URL:
#   app.gohighlevel.com/v2/location/<THIS_PART>/dashboard
# Used by: every tool, via ghl_ids.py. You can also pass --location-id, but you
# rarely need to: funnel and page ids are looked up from names (--funnel/--page),
# so this is usually the only id you ever type.
GHL_LOCATION_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Internal API (backend.leadconnectorhq.com) ───────────────────────────────
# The internal token-id is NOT stored here. It is short-lived (~1h) and is
# captured on demand by get_token.py, which writes it to the file below.
# The PIT does NOT work against the internal API — do not try.

# Where get_token.py writes the captured token-id, and where inject_page.py,
# deploy_workflow.py and create_form.py read it from. Keep it gitignored.
#
# ghl_ids.py also caches funnel/page name -> id lookups in ./.ghl-ids.json for an
# hour so a multi-step build queries once. Not a credential, but it holds your
# account's funnel and page names — gitignored for that reason.
GHL_TOKEN_FILE=.jwt

# Chrome remote-debugging port that get_token.py and create_steps.py attach to.
# You must launch Chrome yourself with --remote-debugging-port=<this> on a
# dedicated --user-data-dir, and log in to GHL by hand once.
GHL_CDP_PORT=9222

# Optional: pass an already-known token-id instead of using the file.
# Overridden by --token on the command line.
# GHL_TOKEN_ID=eyJ...

# ── Build inputs (no credentials below this line) ─────────────────────────────
# Default --templates for ghl_generator.py: the clonable element exemplars
# produced by `capture_funnel.py <url> --exemplars <file>`. Gitignore whatever
# you capture — it carries the source account's ids and copy.
# GHL_ELEMENT_TEMPLATES=exemplars.json

# App host that create_steps.py drives. Change it only if your agency uses a
# white-label domain instead of app.gohighlevel.com.
# GHL_APP_BASE=https://app.gohighlevel.com
